WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.256
Identify, explain and apply the important ideas behind understanding email.

00:00:06.117 --> 00:00:11.036
Recipient: is the person meant to receive an email. Subject: says briefly what the

00:00:11.036 --> 00:00:12.090
message is about.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:17.918
Message body: contains the main written information. Attachment: is a file sent with

00:00:17.918 --> 00:00:21.739
a message. Reply: sends a response to a received message.

00:00:22.617 --> 00:00:27.526
Use an imaginary example or a teacher-approved offline screenshot. Discuss when to

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:33.254
use recipient and subject. Never enter a real password or share private details in

00:00:33.254 --> 00:00:34.073
this activity.
